### Step 2: Determine the number of students in jazz dance

The remaining students (after subtracting those in contemporary) are:

$$
20 - 4 = 16 \text{ students}
$$

25% of these 16 students are in jazz dance.

$$
\text{Jazz students} = 25\% \times 16 = 0.25 \times 16 = 4 \text{ students}
$$

---

### Step 3: Determine the number of students in hip-hop dance

The rest of the students are in hip-hop dance.

$$
\text{Hip-hop students} = 20 - 4 - 4 = 12 \text{ students}
$$

---

### Step 4: Calculate the percentage of students in hip-hop dance

$$
\text{Percentage in hip-hop} = \left( \frac{12}{20} \right) \times 100 = 0.6 \times 100 = 60\%
$$

---

### Final Answer:

$$
\boxed{60}
$$

