To determine how many hours John spends taking care of his dogs in a week, we can break the problem into a few clear steps:

---

### Step 1: Calculate daily time spent per dog
Each dog takes **0.5 hours per day** to walk and care for their business.

- Total number of dogs = 10
- Time spent per dog per day = 0.5 hours

So, total time per day for all dogs:
$$
10 \text{ dogs} \times 0.5 \text{ hours/day} = 5 \text{ hours/day}
$$

---

### Step 2: Calculate weekly time spent
There are **7 days in a week**, so we multiply the daily time by 7:
$$
5 \text{ hours/day} \times 7 \text{ days/week} = 35 \text{ hours/week}
$$

---

