To determine how many hours John spends taking care of his dogs in a week, we can approach the problem in two steps.

---

### Step 1: Calculate the daily hours spent on dogs
John is responsible for 10 dogs, and each dog requires **0.5 hours** per day for walking and taking care of their business.

$$
\text{Daily hours} = 10 \text{ dogs} \times 0.5 \text{ hours per dog} = 5 \text{ hours per day}
$$

