To determine how many pie pieces were taken by the guests, we start by calculating the total number of pie pieces that were available for serving. Grandma Jones baked 5 pies, and each pie was cut into 8 pieces. Therefore, the total number of pieces is:

$$
5 \text{ pies} \times 8 \text{ pieces per pie} = 40 \text{ pieces}
$$

At the end of the evening, 14 pieces of pie remained. To find out how many pieces were taken by the guests, we subtract the remaining pieces from the total number of pieces:

$$
40 \text{ pieces} - 14 \text{ pieces} = 26 \text{ pieces}
$$

Thus, the number of pie pieces taken by the guests is:

$$
\boxed{26}
$$

This calculation is correct based on the information provided in the problem. It follows a straightforward approach of total pieces minus remaining pieces to arrive at the number of pieces taken. The answer is **26**.  
