The problem involves calculating the number of pie pieces taken by guests based on the total number of pieces initially available and the number remaining.

Grandma Jones baked **5 pies**, and each pie was cut into **8 pieces**. Thus, the total number of pie pieces is:
$$
5 \text{ pies} \times 8 \text{ pieces per pie} = 40 \text{ pieces}.
$$

At the end of the evening, **14 pieces** of pie were remaining. To find how many pieces were taken by the guests, subtract the remaining pieces from the total:
$$
