I think that's solid. The steps make sense. The key was setting up the equation correctly. Let me just confirm once more that all the numbers are accounted for. She started with 80, added x, used 220, and had 23 left. So the total post-its after buying is 80 + x. Then subtract 220, equals 23. Solving gives x = 163. All checks out. 

No, I don't see any mistakes here. The answer should be 163.
