So, 4 feet multiplied by 12 inches per foot. Let me calculate that. 4 times 12 is... 48 inches. Okay, so the total length of the wire is 48 inches.

Now, each piece is 6 inches long. To find out how many pieces she can get, I need to divide the total length by the length of each piece. That would be 48 inches divided by 6 inches per piece. Let me do that division.

48 divided by 6. Well, 6 times 8 is 48, right? So 48 divided by 6 is 8. So that would mean she gets 8 pieces.

