$$
15 \text{ floors} \times 8 \text{ units per floor} = 120 \text{ units}
$$

Since 3/4 of the building is occupied, the remaining 1/4 is unoccupied. To find the number of unoccupied units, we calculate:

$$
\frac{1}{4} \times 120 = 30
$$

Thus, the total number of unoccupied units in the building is $\boxed{30}$. 

