   $$
   \text{Distance} = \text{Speed} \times \text{Time} = 10 \, \text{mph} \times 3 \, \text{hours} = 30 \, \text{miles}
   $$

3. **Calculate the time to travel back**: Tok travels back at a speed of 6 miles per hour. The time required to cover the 30-mile distance is:
   $$
   \text{Time} = \frac{\text{Distance}}{\text{Speed}} = \frac{30 \, \text{miles}}{6 \, \text{mph}} = 5 \, \text{hours}
   $$

Thus, the time it takes him to get back is $\boxed{5}$ hours. 
